&lt;li&gt;Master’s degree at &lt;a href="http://web.archive.org/web/20150321125209/http:/www.cegestalt.com/diseno.html"&gt;Centro de Estudios Gestalt&lt;/a&gt;, Veracruz, Mexico&lt;br&gt;
Language: Spanish&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Non-academic: &lt;a href="http://web.archive.org/web/20150321125209/http:/typophile.com/wiki/Font%20Bureau"&gt;Font Bureau&lt;/a&gt; Operated by &lt;a href="http://web.archive.org/web/20150321125209/http:/typophile.com/wiki/David%20Berlow"&gt;Berlow&lt;/a&gt; and others in &lt;a href="http://web.archive.org/web/20150321125209/http:/www.fontbureau.com/info/"&gt;Boston, USA&lt;/a&gt;, with design collaborators including Roger Black, Cyrus Highsmith, Jill Pichotta, and others, as &lt;a href="http://web.archive.org/web/20150321125209/http:/www.typophile.com/node/40360#comment-249066"&gt;suggested by Paul&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;See also: &lt;a href="http://web.archive.org/web/20150321125209/http:/www.typeworkshop.com/index.php?id1=references"&gt;Studying type design&lt;/a&gt; by Luc Devroye.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Veer</title><link>http://typophile-archive.simon-cozens.org/12009/</link><pubDate>Fri, 01 Apr 2005 18:43:00 +0200</pubDate><guid>http://typophile-archive.simon-cozens.org/12009/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;a href="http://web.archive.org/web/20131011023120/http:/typophile.com/wiki/Indices"&gt;Indices&lt;/a&gt; : &lt;a href="http://web.archive.org/web/20131011023120/http:/typophile.com/wiki/Font%20Retailers"&gt;Font Retailers&lt;/a&gt; : Veer&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Veer provides visual elements for use in professional creative work, such as graphic design, motion design, advertising and filmmaking. Products include stock photography, illustration, maps, typefaces, and unique design-related merchandise. Products are showcased on the website &lt;a href="http://web.archive.org/web/20131011023120/http:/www.veer.com/"&gt;veer.com&lt;/a&gt; and in regular direct-mail &lt;a href="http://web.archive.org/web/20131011023120/http:/www.veer.com/ideas/catalogs/"&gt;catalogs&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As part of the company&amp;rsquo;s ongoing involvement in the design community, the creative folks at Veer also maintain &lt;a href="http://web.archive.org/web/20131011023120/http:/blog.veer.com/"&gt;The Skinny&lt;/a&gt;, a lively design and pop-culture influenced weblog. Veer also hosts the type-related animated shorts &lt;a href="http://web.archive.org/web/20131011023120/http:/www.veer.com/ideas/btt/"&gt;&amp;ldquo;Behind the Typeface: Cooper Black&amp;rdquo;&lt;/a&gt; and &lt;a href="http://web.archive.org/web/20131011023120/http:/www.veer.com/ideas/etched/"&gt;&amp;ldquo;Etched in Stone&amp;rdquo;&lt;/a&gt; &amp;ndash; both produced by Typophile regular &lt;a href="http://web.archive.org/web/20131011023120/http:/typophile.com/wiki/Cheshire%20Dave"&gt;Cheshire Dave&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item></channel></rss>